  "worked_solution": "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check this for the above three options:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{64}^{∘}+{73}^{∘}+{98}^{∘}+{124}^{∘}={359}^{∘}\\,X \\\\  &  \\\\ {73}^{∘}+{112}^{∘}+{93}^{∘}+{82}^{∘}={360}^{∘}\\,✓ \\\\  &  \\\\ {80}^{∘}+{140}^{∘}+{49}^{∘}+{84}^{∘}={353}^{∘}\\,X\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only option II could be the angles of a quadrilateral.",
